☁️ 1. Public Cloud (Azure Public Cloud)
What it is:

Azure provides shared infrastructure over the internet.

Azure examples:

Azure Virtual Machines

Azure App Service

Azure SQL Database

Azure Blob Storage

Characteristics:

Multi-tenant

Pay-as-you-go

Managed by Microsoft

Use cases:

Web applications

Startups

Dev/Test environments

📌 Interview line:

“Public cloud resources are owned and managed by Microsoft and shared across multiple customers with logical isolation.”

🏢 2. Private Cloud (Azure Stack / On-Prem)
What it is:

Cloud infrastructure dedicated to one organization.

Azure options:

Azure Stack Hub

Azure Stack HCI

On-premises data center

Characteristics:

Single-tenant

Full control

Higher cost

Use cases:

Banking

Government

Sensitive data

📌 Interview line:

“Private cloud provides dedicated infrastructure with higher security and compliance requirements.”

🔗 3. Hybrid Cloud (Most companies use this)
What it is:

Combination of on-premises + Azure public cloud.

Azure hybrid services:

Azure VPN Gateway

Azure ExpressRoute

Azure Arc

Azure AD (Entra ID)

How it works:

Sensitive data stays on-prem

Scalable workloads run on Azure

Use cases:

Legacy applications

Gradual cloud migration

Disaster recovery

📌 Interview line:

“Hybrid cloud allows organizations to integrate on-premises infrastructure with Azure services for flexibility and scalability.”



